{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q21098971","formula":"C₁₀H₁₄ClN","hill":"C10H14ClN","elements":["H","C","N","Cl"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":14.0,"N":1.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"p-chloromethamphetamine"},"descriptions":{"en":"para-Chloromethamphetamine (PCMA; also known as 4-chloromethamphetamine and 4-CMA; code name Ro 4-6861) is a stimulant that is the N-methyl derivative and prodrug of the neurotoxic drug para-chloroamphetamine (4-CA). It has been found to decrease serotonin in rats. Further investigation into the long-term effects of chloroamphetamines discovered that administration of 4-CMA caused a prolonged reduction in the levels of serotonin and the activity of tryptophan hydroxylase in the brain one month after injection of a single dose of the drug."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":3128,"mass":183.68,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(CC1=CC=C(C=C1)Cl)NC","inchikey":"XXLWNLKEOWWHDC-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-(4-chlorophenyl)-N-methylpropan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3128","atoms":26,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-4.513,"y":-0.248,"z":0.668,"el":"Cl"},{"x":3.595,"y":0.334,"z":-0.294,"el":"N"},{"x":2.228,"y":0.096,"z":0.178,"el":"C"},{"x":1.228,"y":0.443,"z":-0.941,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.216,"y":0.27,"z":-0.537,"el":"C"},{"x":2.12,"y":-1.361,"z":0.628,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.835,"y":-0.954,"z":-0.737,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.896,"y":1.337,"z":0.028,"el":"C"},{"x":4.555,"y":0.072,"z":0.765,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.169,"y":-1.115,"z":-0.364,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.231,"y":1.176,"z":0.401,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.867,"y":-0.05,"z":0.205,"el":"C"},{"x":2.018,"y":0.745,"z":1.039,"el":"H"},{"x":1.428,"y":-0.17,"z":-1.831,"el":"H"},{"x":1.381,"y":1.482,"z":-1.267,"el":"H"},{"x":2.77,"y":-1.594,"z":1.478,"el":"H"},{"x":2.356,"y":-2.055,"z":-0.187,"el":"H"},{"x":1.114,"y":-1.596,"z":0.986,"el"